  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nServices\nFrontend build\n\n// Service\n\nFrontend build \n\nYour product's interface, from the first component to the production deploy.\n\nPrice\nFrom €9,500\nTimeline\n4 to 8 weeks\nStart this project\n\nOpens the contact form with this service picked. Nothing is sent yet.\n\n// Scope\n\nI join your team or work from a design file and take the frontend the whole way: architecture, components, state, tests and the release pipeline. You get working software every week, not a big reveal at the end.\n\nIncludes\n\nArchitecture note before any code\nTyped component library\nTests on every critical flow\nA handover call and written docs\n\n// How it runs\n\nFrom the first note to the handover. \n\n01\nWeek 0\n\nArchitecture note\n\nTwo pages: routes, data flow, state, what gets tested and what does not. You sign it off before any code exists.\n\n02\nWeek 1\n\nFirst deploy\n\nA real screen on a real URL behind a login, with CI, a preview per pull request and the performance budget switched on.\n\n03\nWeeks 2 to 6\n\nOne flow a week\n\nEach flow is finished before the next one starts: components, empty and error states, tests. A written update every Friday.\n\n04\nLast week\n\nHandover\n\nDocs in the repository, a recorded walkthrough and a call with whoever maintains it next.\n\n// Questions\n\nAsked about this service. \n01\nDo you need finished designs?\n\nNo. Wireframes and a brand guide are enough. I settle the details in the browser, where they can be tested on a real phone.\n\n02\nWho owns the code?\n03\nWhat if the scope changes?\n\n// Other services\n\nFrom €3,200\nPerformance audit\nA measured list of what is slow, why, and what each fix is worth.\nFrom €12,000\nDesign system\nOne set of tokens and components your whole team actually uses.\nFrom €6,400 a month\nTeam embed\nA senior frontend developer inside your team, three days a week.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n--:--\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.",
